{"qid":"Q420759","names":["Second Bulgarian Empire"],"title":"Second Bulgarian Empire","endonym":{"native":"Второ българско царство","lang":"bg"},"capsule":"The Second Bulgarian Empire was re-established in 1185 when the brothers Asen and Peter led a successful rebellion against Byzantine rule, founding a new Tarnovo-based tsardom that Kaloyan (r. 1197–1207) expanded by defeating a Fourth Crusade army at Adrianople in 1205 and killing Emperor Baldwin I. Tsar Ivan Asen II (r. 1218–1241) brought the empire to its greatest extent, controlling most of the Balkans from the Adriatic to the Black Sea, before Mongol pressure and internal fragmentation progressively weakened it. Bulgarian resistance collapsed when Ottoman forces under Sultan Bayezid I defeated Tsar Ivan Shishman, who was captured and executed; Tarnovo fell in 1393 and the last fortresses held out until around 1396–1422.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. The empire's core Bulgarian lands are well attested, but its shifting frontier regions—particularly in Thrace and Macedonia—varied substantially by decade and are only approximately reconstructed.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: Second Bulgarian Empire","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Second-Bulgarian-Empire"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Second Bulgarian Empire","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Bulgarian_Empire"},{"label":"John Fine, The Late Medieval Balkans (University of Michigan Press, 1987)","url":"https://archive.org/details/latemedievalbalk0000fine"}],"britannica":"place/Second-Bulgarian-empire","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Second Bulgarian Empire","rulers":[{"qid